# Responsive Standards

- Build mobile-first layouts.
- Ensure all pages work correctly on:
  - mobile (360px)
  - tablet (768px)
  - desktop (1024px+)

## Layout

- Use flexible layouts.
- Prefer flex/grid over fixed positioning.
- Avoid fixed widths that break responsiveness.
- Use wrapping and overflow handling properly.

## Tables

For tables:
- Prefer responsive cards on mobile when appropriate.
- Otherwise provide horizontal scrolling.
- Never allow tables to overflow the viewport invisibly.

## Typography

- Ensure text remains readable on small screens.
- Avoid oversized typography on mobile.
- Maintain proper spacing and touch targets.

## Touch usability

- Ensure clickable elements are easy to tap.
- Avoid tiny buttons or crowded controls.